---

# [Requirements]($heading.id('requirements'))

- Zig 0.17.0 or newer.
- Nothing else at build time: the checker needs no running database.
- At runtime, SQLite is bundled with zqlite; PostgreSQL needs a server
  between 15 and 18.

# [Fetch the package]($heading.id('fetch-the-package'))

```console
$ zig fetch --save git+https://github.com/westack-it/sqlz
```

This adds `sqlz` to `build.zig.zon`. sqlz has no tagged release yet, so the
dependency pins a commit on `main`.

# [Choose backends]($heading.id('choose-backends'))

Backends are build options of the dependency. All are off by default:

| Option | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `sqlite` | fetch and build the zqlite runtime adapter |
| `postgres` | fetch and build the pg.zig runtime adapter |
| `postgres_tls` | enable driver TLS; requires `postgres` |

```zig
const sqlz_dep = b.dependency("sqlz", .{
    .sqlite = true,
    .postgres = true,
});
```

A disabled driver is never fetched, imported, compiled or linked. There is no
default backend and no runtime `AnyDatabase`: code uses `sqlz.sqlite` or
`sqlz.postgres` directly.

# [Register a project]($heading.id('register-a-project'))

```zig
const sqlz_build = @import("sqlz");

const tool = sqlz_build.addTool(b, .{ .dependency = sqlz_dep });
const db = tool.addProject(.{
    .name = "app",
    .config = b.path("sqlz.ziggy"),
    .runtime = .{ .sqlite = true },
});

exe.root_module.addImport("sqlz", db.runtime_module);
exe.root_module.addImport("queries", db.queries_module);
exe.step.dependOn(db.check_step);
```

`.runtime` is the subset of enabled backends this project executes against.
Naming a backend the dependency was built without panics at configure time.
A build can register several projects with one tool.

>[]($block.attrs('note'))
>`addProject` registers every `.sql`, `.zig` and `.ziggy` file under the
>project directory as a build input, so adding or editing a query re-runs the
>checker.
